panvk: build Mesa's Vulkan driver for the Mali on Darwin (iOS and macOS), over src/hakios-drm

Applied by tools/mk-panvk.sh only, after tools/mesa/*.patch, to Mesa 25.0.7 (Mesa's own licence,
MIT, applies to the lines it adds). Written for Scion; no other project's patch was used.
  - meson.build: the libdrm stand-in (src/hakios-drm) for PanVK as well, and HAVE_LIBDRM with it,
    so that vk_instance.c lists the devices hakios.drm.c's drmGetDevices2() gives (the Mali).
  - src/panfrost/vulkan/meson.build: Mach-O has no undefined weak symbols resolving to NULL at
    static link time; the entrypoint tables' weak references are left to dyld (-undefined
    dynamic_lookup), which binds a weak reference it cannot find to NULL. mk-panvk.sh refuses the
    library if anything but a weak reference is left so.
  - panvk_instance.c: Mach-O has no GNU build-id; the image's LC_UUID stands in for it.
  - panvk_physical_device.c: no <sys/sysinfo.h> or <sys/sysmacros.h>; total memory from
    os_get_total_physical_memory().
  - vk_image.h/.c: drm_format_mod (VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier, which PanVK uses for its
    own tiling choices) on Apple as on Linux and the BSDs.
  - src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build: wsi_common.c without HAVE_LIBDRM on Darwin, since wsi_common_drm.c
    (dma-buf, KMS) is not built there; otherwise its nine calls into it are left undefined.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1716,7 +1716,7 @@
